\caption(The learned scalar count is independent of spatial image size; shared filters are reused at every location.)

> The executed MNIST architecture

The original model has \((9\cdot1\cdot8+8)+(9\cdot8\cdot4+4)+
(9\cdot4\cdot8+8)+(9\cdot8\cdot1+1)=741\) learned scalars in eight tensors.
A 28 by 28 image requires 225,792 convolution multiply-accumulate pairs per forward pass,
excluding bias, activations, pooling and repetition. For fixed channel counts, arithmetic and
activation storage scale linearly with the number of image pixels.

The trace below executes a single image with Flow style and block detail, grouping the executed operations at six named boundaries.
The decoder-stage labels explicitly include repetition and their learned convolution. Shapes use shared linear spatial
and channel scales with a two-pixel visibility floor and at most six sampled planes. Glyphs
aggregate tensors; labels retain exact dimensions. This is an architecture shape probe rather
than a separate fit. The canonical `models::ConvolutionalAutoencoder` and
`models::ConvolutionalDecoder` preserve the original layer names and checkpoint layout.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/convolutional_architecture.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  n::ParameterStore p(1801);
  n::Module         model(
      [&](const n::Tensor& input) {
        const auto net = n::models::ConvolutionalAutoencoder(p, input);
        n::model_stage("Conv 3×3 1→8 / ReLU", input, net.conv1);
        n::model_stage("Mean pool 2×2", net.conv1, net.pool1);
        n::model_stage("Conv 3×3 8→4 / ReLU", net.pool1, net.conv2);
        n::model_stage("Mean pool 2×2 / code", net.conv2, net.code);
        n::model_stage("Repeat 2 / conv 4→8 / ReLU", net.code, net.decoder1);
        return n::model_stage("Repeat 2 / conv 8→1 / sigmoid", net.decoder1, net.reconstruction);
      },
      "Spatial autoencoder: 28 × 28 × 1 to 7 × 7 × 4 and back");
  n::ModelPlotOptions options;
  options.style                 = n::ModelPlotStyle::Flow;
  options.detail                = n::ModelPlotDetail::Blocks;
  options.sizing.spatial_scale  = n::ModelPlotScale::Linear;
  options.sizing.channel_scale  = n::ModelPlotScale::Linear;
  options.sizing.minimum_extent = 2;
  options.sizing.max_planes     = 6;
  const auto figure             = model.plot(n::zeros({1, 28, 28, 1}), options);
  if (p.count() != 741 || figure.parameter_count() != 741)
    return 1;
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  figure.save_svg("build/convolutional_architecture.svg");
  std::print("{} learned tensors; {} learned scalars.\n", p.size(), p.count());
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
8 learned tensors; 741 learned scalars.
\image(figures/convolutional_architecture.svg)
// result_end

\caption(The full reconstruction path reduces spatial extent twice and restores it twice, with no skip connection. All four convolution kernels are independent.)
\alttext(A left to right spatial autoencoder trace shows encoder feature maps, a 7 by 7 by 4 code and the decoder restoring 28 by 28 grayscale pixels.)

> A genuine-MNIST fit with visible updates

The native dataset API prepares the original disjoint, class-balanced MNIST pools: 1,000 fitting,
200 validation and 200 held-out images. Every pool contains equal counts for digits 0 through 9;
labels only order the later gallery. Original source IDs and the dataset manifest are retained.
Input images are Float32 NHWC probabilities. He-uniform initialization is used on the three
ReLU convolutions, Glorot-uniform on the output and zeros for every bias. Seed 1801 initializes
the model; seed 1807 determines minibatch order. Adam uses learning rate 0.003 and its standard
0.9/0.999 moments and epsilon 1e-8.

Each of three epochs visits all 1,000 fitting images once in batches of 32, including a final
batch of eight: 96 updates in total. The code retains the complete optimizer loop. Validation
MSE, accumulated in Float64 from the Float32 predictions as in the source, selects a checkpoint;
test images do not enter training or selection. Fitting losses are pre-update minibatch values,
whereas validation uses the post-epoch weights. Every initial gradient tensor is checked for a
finite, nonzero norm. Initial, first-update, each epoch and selected parameters are saved.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/convolutional_learning.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const std::filesystem::path cache = dm::datasets::data_home();
  dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("mnist-assets", cache.string());
  const auto pools = n::models::LoadSaliency(cache / "saliency");
  std::filesystem::copy_file(
      cache / "saliency" / "manifest.json",
      "build/convolutional_data_manifest.json",
      std::filesystem::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
  const auto        fit = pools[0].images, validation = pools[1].images, test = pools[2].images;
  n::ParameterStore p(1801);
  {
    n::NoGradGuard guard;
    n::models::ConvolutionalAutoencoder(p, n::zeros({1, 28, 28, 1}));
  }
  if (p.count() != 741 || p.size() != 8)
    return 1;
  p.save("build/convolutional_initial.npz");
  const auto         initial = n::models::ConvolutionalAutoencoder(p, test).reconstruction.detach();
  n::OptimizerConfig config;
  config.kind = n::OptimizerKind::Adam;
  n::Optimizer        optimizer(p, .003, config);
  n::BatchOrder       batches(1000, 32, 1807);
  double              best     = std::numeric_limits<double>::infinity();
  int                 selected = 0, updates = 0;
  std::vector<double> epochs, training, valid, gradient_norms;
  std::print("| epoch | fitting pre-update MSE | validation MSE |\n|---:|---:|---:|\n");
  for (int epoch = 1; epoch <= 3; ++epoch) {
    batches.begin_epoch();
    double total = 0;
    int    seen  = 0;
    for (;;) {
      const auto rows = batches.next();
      if (rows.empty())
        break;
      const auto input = n::take_rows(fit, rows);
      const auto net   = n::models::ConvolutionalAutoencoder(p, input);
      const auto loss  = n::mse(net.reconstruction, input);
      if (updates == 0) {
        n::GradOptions keep;
        keep.retain_graph         = true;
        const auto      gradients = n::grad(loss, p.parameters(), keep);
        n::NamedTensors saved{{"input", input}};
        for (std::size_t i = 0; i < gradients.size(); ++i) {
          const double norm = n::sqrt(n::sum(n::square(gradients[i]))).item();
          if (!std::isfinite(norm) || norm <= 0)
            return 1;
          gradient_norms.push_back(norm);
          saved.emplace_back(p.names()[i], gradients[i]);
        }
        n::save_npz("build/convolutional_first_gradients.npz", saved);
      }
      const double value = loss.item();
      if (!std::isfinite(value) || value < 0)
        return 1;
      total += rows.size() * value;
      seen += int(rows.size());
      optimizer.minimize(loss);
      if (updates == 0)
        p.save("build/convolutional_first_update.npz");
      ++updates;
    }
    n::NoGradGuard guard;
    const auto     prediction = n::models::ConvolutionalAutoencoder(p, validation).reconstruction;
    const double   score =
        n::mse(n::cast(prediction, n::DType::Float64), n::cast(validation, n::DType::Float64))
            .item();
    if (seen != 1000 || !std::isfinite(score))
      return 1;
    p.save("build/convolutional_epoch" + std::to_string(epoch) + ".npz");
    if (score < best) {
      best     = score;
      selected = epoch;
      p.save("build/convolutional_best.npz");
    }
    epochs.push_back(epoch);
    training.push_back(total / seen);
    valid.push_back(score);
    std::print("| {} | {:.9f} | {:.9f} |\n", epoch, total / seen, score);
  }
  if (updates != 96)
    return 1;
  std::print("\n| parameter | initial gradient L2 norm |\n|---|---:|\n");
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < gradient_norms.size(); ++i)
    std::print("| {} | {:.8f} |\n", p.names()[i], gradient_norms[i]);
  n::ParameterStore deployed(1801);
  deployed.load("build/convolutional_best.npz", false);
  const auto     before = deployed.flatten();
  n::NoGradGuard guard;
  const auto     net      = n::models::ConvolutionalAutoencoder(deployed, test);
  const auto     decoded  = n::models::ConvolutionalDecoder(deployed, net.code).reconstruction;
  const auto     repeated = n::models::ConvolutionalAutoencoder(deployed, test).reconstruction;
  const auto     single =
      n::models::ConvolutionalAutoencoder(deployed, n::take_rows(test, {0})).reconstruction;
  if (n::max(n::abs(decoded - net.reconstruction)).item() != 0 ||
      n::max(n::abs(repeated - net.reconstruction)).item() != 0 ||
      n::max(n::abs(single - n::take_rows(net.reconstruction, {0}))).item() > 2e-6)
    return 1;
  const auto mean = n::broadcast_to(
      n::cast(n::mean(n::cast(fit, n::DType::Float64), {0}, true), n::DType::Float32),
      test.shape());
  const auto pooled = n::upsample_nearest(n::avg_pool2d(test, 4, 4), 4);
  const auto zero =
      n::models::ConvolutionalDecoder(deployed, n::zeros({200, 7, 7, 4})).reconstruction;
  const auto shuffled_code =
      n::concat({n::slice_axis(net.code, 0, 1, 200), n::slice_axis(net.code, 0, 0, 1)}, 0);
  const auto shuffled = n::models::ConvolutionalDecoder(deployed, shuffled_code).reconstruction;
  if (before != deployed.flatten())
    return 1;
  std::print(
      "\nSelected epoch {}: validation MSE {:.9f}; {} updates.\n\n| held-out predictor | MSE "
      "|\n|---|---:|\n",
      selected,
      best,
      updates);
  for (const auto& [name, prediction] : std::vector<std::pair<std::string, n::Tensor>>{
           {"initial network", initial},
           {"fitting pixel mean", mean},
           {"4×4 pool/repeat", pooled},
           {"selected autoencoder", net.reconstruction},
           {"zero code", zero},
           {"cyclically shifted code", shuffled}})
    std::print(
        "| {} | {:.9f} |\n",
        name,
        n::mse(n::cast(prediction, n::DType::Float64), n::cast(test, n::DType::Float64)).item());
  const auto probe  = n::take_rows(test, {0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7});
  const auto stages = n::models::ConvolutionalAutoencoder(deployed, probe);
  n::save_npz(
      "build/convolutional_results.npz",
      {{"fit_images", fit},
       {"validation_images", validation},
       {"test_images", test},
       {"fit_ids", pools[0].source},
       {"validation_ids", pools[1].source},
       {"test_ids", pools[2].source},
       {"test_labels", pools[2].labels},
       {"code", net.code},
       {"reconstruction", net.reconstruction},
       {"initial", initial},
       {"mean", mean},
       {"pooled", pooled},
       {"zero", zero},
       {"shuffled", shuffled},
       {"probe", probe},
       {"conv1", stages.conv1},
       {"pool1", stages.pool1},
       {"conv2", stages.conv2},
       {"probe_code", stages.code},
       {"decoder1", stages.decoder1},
       {"probe_reconstruction", stages.reconstruction}});
  auto plot = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  plot.lines(epochs, training, "Fitting, pre-update", {37, 99, 235}, 2.)
      .lines(epochs, valid, "Validation, post-epoch", {220, 38, 38}, 2.)
      .x_label("epoch")
      .y_label("mean squared pixel error")
      .title("Spatial autoencoder: Adam 0.003, 96 updates")
      .save_svg("build/convolutional_learning.svg");
}
```
