\caption(Fitting and validation errors over three epochs. The two curves evaluate different parameter states.)
\alttext(Fitting pre-update loss and post-epoch validation loss decrease across three epochs.)

Epoch 3 is selected with validation MSE 0.01834. The held-out learned reconstruction gives
MSE 0.01778, about 73.8% below the fitting mean's 0.06780 and 57.6% below the pool/repeat
control's 0.04195. Shifting codes raises MSE to 0.09363, and zeroing them raises it to 0.14243;
this decoder uses the sample-specific spatial code. The reconstructions retain recognizable
strokes but smooth fine details. These controls demonstrate dependence on the input, not the
semantic quality of its representation.

The fitting mean is the squared-error-optimal constant predictor. The pool/repeat control uses
49 input-dependent numbers per image, versus the learned code's 196; it is not a matched-capacity
competitor. Zero codes test the decoder without sample information. Cyclically shifting the 200
codes preserves their marginal distribution but breaks their pairing with the target images.
Neither control is refitted. The fresh checkpoint restore, separate decoder call, repeated
inference and single-versus-batch comparison check deployment, and all eight learned tensors
remain unchanged throughout evaluation.

The gallery chooses the first held-out occurrence of each digit, without quality filtering.
Its rows are original, learned reconstruction, absolute error, fitting mean, pool/repeat,
untrained network, zero-code decoder and shifted-code decoder. The same [0,1] grayscale applies
to every panel, including the unamplified error row. Labels order images only; this is not a
classification experiment and has no confusion matrix.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/convolutional_reconstructions.png", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::map<std::string, n::Tensor> a;
  for (const auto& [name, value] : n::load_npz("build/convolutional_results.npz"))
    a.emplace(name, value);
  const auto                labels = a.at("test_labels").to_vector<int>();
  const auto                ids    = a.at("test_ids").to_vector<int>();
  std::vector<std::int64_t> rows;
  for (int digit = 0; digit < 10; ++digit) {
    const auto found = std::find(labels.begin(), labels.end(), digit);
    if (found == labels.end())
      return 1;
    rows.push_back(found - labels.begin());
  }
  std::vector<n::Tensor> panels;
  for (const auto& name :
       {"test_images",
        "reconstruction",
        "error",
        "mean",
        "pooled",
        "initial",
        "zero",
        "shuffled"}) {
    const auto values = std::string(name) == "error"
                            ? n::abs(a.at("reconstruction") - a.at("test_images"))
                            : a.at(name);
    panels.push_back(n::take_rows(values, rows));
  }
  n::save_image_grid(
      n::concat(panels, 0), "build/convolutional_reconstructions.png", 10, 0, 1, 2, .8, 3);
  std::print("| digit | original MNIST source ID |\n|---:|---:|\n");
  for (int digit = 0; digit < 10; ++digit)
    std::print("| {} | {} |\n", digit, ids[rows[digit]]);
}
```
